LANGUAGE English
DEBUG OFF

BOOK DvmClosePortal ORDERED KEEP LOOPED
    IF goal != goalClosePortal THEN EXIT

    PAGE Page1
        BUTTON "Open the book" AFTER "Table of Contents"

        PROLOG "The De Vermis Mysterium looks old and worn with time."

        TEXT "
            Table of Contents

            You open the book. On the inside
            cover, someone--probably {c:EventChosenInvestigator}>s father--
            scrawled a note that reads, <<Only my descendants will be able to
            read this book, and only at the appointed hour. I have seen to
            this.>> 
			
			You puzzle over this for a moment, then turn to the first page.
			It>s a table of contents. The book seems to be full of spells and
			rituals. You scan down to find something about portals. Maybe
			<<Travel, page 72>>?

            {qst:FirstTimeRead}, gain 1 {clue}.
        "
    END PAGE

    PAGE Page2
        PROLOG "
            This is a spell book and {c:EventChosenInvestigator}
			may have... abilities. Sarah is pushing to find something
			about closing portals.
        "
        
        BUTTON "Turn to page 72" AFTER "Portal"

        TEXT "
            You flip through the pages to find the <<Travel>> section on
            page 72. The first entry is for portals.

            Portals
            
            You read through an overview of the spell and skim past the opening
            ritual, including the list of materials needed to open one. Behind
			it is a closing ritual: how to close a portal that has already been
			cast.
            
            There is a list of materials and artifacts needed.
            The list includes a dagger, chalice, human skull, and
            various herbs. There>s also mention of an <<elder sign>>
            but you aren>t sure what that is. From what you saw earlier in the
			book, these materials seem similar to what is needed to open a
			portal.
            
            <i>I wonder if they actually have these already?</i> you hope to
            yourself. 
        "
    END PAGE

    PAGE Page3
        PROLOG "Closing a portal is going to require a lot of work."

        BUTTON "Read the next page" AFTER "Tools"
    
        TEXT "
            Dagger
        
            You flip the page. Here the book goes into detail about the
            knife needed to close the portal. It sounds beautiful,
			but you wonder where you would find something like that. Next is
			the process of empowering the blade. When you look at
			the incantation, it is written in a language you cannot read
			and, when you try, no sound comes from your mouth. Apparently,
			you will use this knife to draw blood for the ritual. Your blood.

            Elder Sign
        
            According to the book, once the portal has manifested, it is weak
			and unstable. An elder sign is used to stabilize it.
			Either way, an
			elder sign is needed to close it. There is a drawing
			of one here, so now you know what to look for. There is
			another incatation you cannot understand or even sound out.

            {qst:FirstTimeRead}, gain 1 {clue}.
        "
    END PAGE

    PAGE Page4
        PROLOG "
            Each tool seems to need special attention. This will require more
            study.
        "
        
        BUTTON "Read the next page" AFTER "Sacrifice"
    
        TEXT "
            Sacrifice

            The next page delves into the importance of personal sacrifice.
            For this ritual, the sacrifice is small:  a few drops of your own
            blood. You shudder as you read about using even more of your blood
			for this.
			
			You remember it saying a person is required to make the portal.
			You wonder who they might choose.

            {qst:FirstTimeRead}, suffer 1 Horror ({will} negates).
        "
		
		IF readJournalPage5 THEN TEXT "
            Sacrifice

            The next page delves into the importance of personal sacrifice.
            For this ritual, the sacrifice is small:  a few drops of your own
            blood. You shudder as you read about using even more of your blood
			for this.
			
			You remember it saying a person is required to make the portal.
			<i>It must be the boy,</i> you say out loud and startle yourself
			when you hear your own voice.

            {qst:FirstTimeRead}, suffer 1 Horror ({will} negates).
		"
    END PAGE
    
    PAGE Page5
        PROLOG "
            A look of concern and disgust on your face, you turn the page.
        "

        BUTTON "Read the next page" AFTER "Commentary"

        TEXT "
            Commentary

            Finally, there is commentary and advice. One section discusses ley
            lines and how they allow you to draw more power for the ritual.
            Determining the preferred dates and times for the ritual is also
            discussed, with a full moon being the most important part.
        
            In the margin are notes about a place under the house that aligns
            with a ley line; there is also a list of years that would be good
            for the ritual, and specific dates that are the best. Today is on
            the list.
        "

        IF readAboutBoy THEN TEXT "
            Commentary

            Finally, there is commentary and advice. One section discusses ley
            lines and how to use them draw more power for the ritual.
            Calculating the date and time for the ritual is also discussed,
            with a full moon being the most important.
        
            In the margin are notes about a place under the house that aligns
            with a ley line; there is also a list of years that would be good
            for the ritual, and specific dates that are the best. Today is on
            the list.

            <i>The boy must be under the house somewhere,</i> you think to
            yourself.
        "

		// ??? Why is this here
        // TRIGGER @FoundCellHoleViaJournal
    END PAGE
    
    EPILOG
        TEXT "
            <i>Maybe I need to explore a bit more to figure out what I need to
            do to stop this madness,</i> you think to yourself.
        "
    
        IF exploredTortureChamber THEN TEXT "
            Now you know where the ritual will be performed and what is needed.
            You must stop your uncle!
        "

        IF readJournalPage4 THEN TEXT "
            You cannot allow a child to be sacrificed for this evil. You must
            find the artifacts before they start the ritual and, if you can, 
            save the boy.
        "
    END EPILOG
END BOOK